                            {
                                "id": "0,7,0,0",
                                "type": 4,
                                "elements": "If more than one expression appears on a single line in the calculator block, they will be visually separated by bounding boxes, which helps us understand that they are different expressions. For example, here the expression \"-cos(c)\" is outside the assignment statement and therefore isn't involved in the calculation of the y function. This is because the cursor was outside the assignment statement when the \"-\" was entered.",
